      "object 0": {
        "ID": 0,
        "gui": {
          "x": "40.0",
          "y": "20.0",
          "w": "640"
        },
        "parms": "# change togedge — only what changes\nchange passes a number on only when it differs from the one before, so a stream that repeats itself sends each value once. Its two other outlets send 1 when the value leaves 0 and when it comes back to 0. togedge watches for those same two moments and bangs a separate outlet for each.\nMax's change compares whole numbers unless its argument is a float, and Max's togedge truncates a float, so 0.5 counts as 0. Here both take the number as it is: 0.5 counts as on.",
